# RecallSync — CLI first

For RecallSync reads/writes (leads, campaigns, agents, conversations, etc.), **use the
`recallsync` CLI via Shell** — not raw REST, not Prisma.

## Run from AIOS repo root

```bash
node scripts/recallsync-cli.mjs --json leads list --page-size 10
node scripts/recallsync-cli.mjs campaign leads --id <campaignId>
node scripts/recallsync-cli.mjs conversation messages --id <conversationId>
```

The wrapper loads `.env` / `.env.local` and maps `RECALL_API_KEY` → `RECALLSYNC_API_KEY`.
**Set `RECALLSYNC_BASE_URL` in `.env.local`** to your hosted RecallSync domain (same URL
you export in terminal). If unset, it defaults to `http://localhost:3000/api/rest` — that
only works when `recallsync-app` is running locally on port 3000.

```bash
# .env.local (fusionsyncai repo)
RECALL_API_KEY=your_key
RECALLSYNC_BASE_URL=https://<your-agency-domain>/api/rest
```

Always pass **`--json`** so output is parseable.

## MCP tool → CLI map (common)

| MCP tool | CLI |
|----------|-----|
| `get-leads` | `leads list` |
| `get-lead` | `leads get --id` |
| `create-lead` | `leads create --name ... --body '{...}'` |
| `find-lead` | `leads find --email ...` |
| `get-all-campaigns` | `campaign list` |
| `get-campaign-leads` | `campaign leads --id` |
| `get-conversation-messages` | `conversation messages --id` |
| `create-conversation-message` | `conversation create-message --body '{...}'` |

Full command list: `recallsync --help`

## Do

- Prefer CLI when MCP hangs, times out, or is unavailable.
- Use `--json` on every command for agent sessions.
- If a command is missing, add it in `recallsync-cli` (recall repo) or fall back to MCP.

## Don't

- **Never** `curl` / `fetch` / `axios` to `*/api/rest/*` directly.
- **Never** hardcode bearer tokens in commands — the wrapper reads `.env.local`.
- **Never** use Prisma against RecallSync DB from AIOS.

## Fallback

If `recallsync` is not on PATH (`command not found`), use MCP tools
(`project-0-fusionsyncai-recallsync-primary`). See `recallsync-mcp-run`.
